{
	title: "Concurrent EDITs of one lease combine; scripts/action shows the model's view",
	spec: "An EDIT naming a version Hal's own EDITs replaced still applies when its ranges miss every change made since: lease.carry shifts its ranges through the remembered edits (the last 32 of the 256 most recently edited files) into the current version, so a round's EDITs of one READ combine in any order. A range overlapping such a change fails, writing nothing, with the current lines around it; a change outside Hal breaks the chain and the lease is just stale. scripts/action is a human's model-view REPL: it prints the system prompt Hal would send for the cwd, then runs typed Action text through the real tool modules and prints each result; an incomplete action continues on the next line, an empty line sends it. It uses a throwaway Hal home with a copy of the config, so real sessions stay untouched.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Batching a round's EDITs by timing was rejected: approval can delay one call past any window, so the chain of Hal's own edits (keyed by resolved path, hash before -> after) carries ranges instead. Importing auth.ts before host.ts trips an existing import cycle (also breaks src/host/turns-retry.test.ts); scripts/action imports host.ts first."
	],
	needs: ['3fv'],
